# mutgap4_sys_tracker_merge_then_unmap: A map that overlaps the end of one run and the start of the next is merged into the first, and the clean-up that follows trims the next run to what the merged run leaves of it (RunBlock::add): runs [0, 2) and [3, 5), then a map of [1, 4) leaves [0, 4) and [4, 5). An unmap of [3, 4) then trims [0, 4) to [0, 3), so a probe of page 3 maps it again (one map_memory call), and a probe of [0, 3) and of [4, 5) maps nothing. Blocks only.
